# The NIGHT daypart is a midnight-crossing BAND in colloquial clock usage,
# not a uniform +12 PM shift: "pukul satu malam" (one at night) is 01:00,
# "pukul sebelas malam" (eleven at night) is 23:00, twelve is midnight
# 00:00.  Small hours 1..5 stay AM, evening hours 6..11 are PM, twelve is
# midnight (band-split in resolver _clock_hms).  Evening "malam" opens at
# 19:00 (CLDR ms night [19:00, 00:00), transcribed in chronologia/
# dayparts.py); the small hours read as "malam" colloquially.  Source:
# Wiktionary, malam (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/malam#Malay).
malam
